Done. Here's a summary of the implementation:

---

### Usage

**Default fallback UI:**
```tsx
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Custom fallback:**
```tsx
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(error, retry) => (
  <MyCustomFallback message={error.message} onRetry={retry} />
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**With external error logging (e.g. Sentry):**
```tsx
<ErrorBoundary onError={(error, info) => Sentry.captureException(error, { extra: info })}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

---

### Key design decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| Class component | `getDerivedStateFromError` / `componentDidCatch` have no hook equivalents |
| `retry` resets state to `null` | Allows React to re-render the child tree from scratch |
| `fallback` prop is a render function | Passes `error` and `retry` to caller without extra context wiring |
| `onError` prop | Decouples logging from the component; caller can use Sentry, Datadog, etc. |
| `role="alert"` on fallback div | Screen readers announce the error without focus management |
